# prepush_scan.sh — GENERIC term patterns (DATA, read by scripts/prepush_scan.sh §1).
#
# One extended regex per line, matched case-insensitively against tracked
# content. Blank lines and lines beginning with '#' are ignored; the scan joins
# the remaining lines into one alternation.
#
# This tracked file holds only GENERIC patterns: shapes of private network
# names that never belong in a public tree. Deployment-specific terms (prior
# host codenames, private host names, vendor and model codenames) live in the
# git-ignored `.prepush_terms.local` beside this file, same format, read when
# present — a public file that listed them would itself publish them. A
# checkout without the local file still runs the generic patterns and says so.
#
# Both files are EXCLUDED from the scan (they necessarily contain the terms).

# Private-network DNS suffixes (LAN / home / mesh-VPN names).
[a-z0-9-]\.(lan|home\.arpa|localdomain)\b
\.ts\.net\b
